The vsock port the daemon of a guest serves the api on, for the daemon of its
hypervisor to reach it with no network and no credential, none when zero.

Set it on a guest only: the guest needs a vsock device, and answers the
hypervisor alone. A connection from a reserved source port, which only a
privileged process of the hypervisor can bind, is granted `root`, as the
hypervisor is root on its guests anyway. Any other connection of the hypervisor
has to authenticate, and the other guests are dropped.

Takes effect at the next daemon start.
